# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Name | Provider | Recommended use | Unique benefits | Cost per execution (RUs) |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| QUICK-PDE<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/colibritd-pde)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/colibritd-pde/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/eylihre0nf2lskzteyabd7y7v7cu5bb3)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/colibritd-quick-pde-eula.pdf) | ColibriTD            | Use quantum computation for multi-physics PDEs.<br/><br/>Prepare simulation workflows for quantum hardware, while keeping full control over both quantum and physical modeling parameters.                     | Offers a robust hybrid VQA framework that delivers precise, scalable PDE solutions through advanced solution encoding and spectral methods, making it an ideal entry point for teams trying to build quantum-ready simulation capabilities. | S: 1<br/> M: 5<br/>L: 10 |\n"
"| Quantum Portfolio Optimizer <br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/global-data-quantum-optimizer)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/global-data-quantum-optimizer/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/t9tj2t8ey8hh1iep3jr88yzlqbqdvq78)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/global-data-quantum-quantum-portfolio-optimizer-eula.pdf)  | Global Data Quantum  | Workloads for financial optimization, seeking optimal portfolio strategies over time while minimizing risk and maximizing returns, enabling trading strategy back-testing.                                   | Solves combinatorial optimization problems through a highly specialized adaptation of the VQE quantum algorithm for this financial use case, using optimized execution strategies and optimizers, along with noise-aware error mitigation techniques tailored to portfolio optimization. | S: 5<br/> M: 40<br/>L: 400 |\n"
"| HI-VQE Chemistry<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/qunova-chemistry)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/qunova-chemistry/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/7d36ty2r5ecmnnu1bvk4kxx5grbz2mwz)   | Qunova Computing     | Workloads in computational chemistry, molecular simulation, materials science, or any Hamiltonian simulation that require solving many-body electronic structure problems.                                   | Solves molecular electronic structures by using enhanced SQD with achieving chemical accuracy (1 kcal/mol, 1.6 mHa) for problems modeled with 40 to 60 qubits, outperforming some classical solutions on supercomputers or standard SQD in convergence speed or accuracy, respectively, by orders of magnitude.                                                                                                                                               | N/A |\n"
"| Iskay Quantum Optimizer<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/kipu-optimization)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/kipu-optimization/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/h7ocmsqgwjuj493b46m1nrkqkazh4g4j)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/kipu-quantum-functions-eula.pdf) | Kipu Quantum         | Optimization workloads such as  scheduling, logistics, routing, and QUBO/HUBO problems. <br/><br/>  | Integrated tunable classical pre- and post-processing methods for the quantum optimization routine. <br/><br/>Delivers runtime advantage over classical solvers (CPLEX, simulated annealing, and tabu search) on selected HUBO benchmarks. <br/><br/>Market Split `ms_5_100`, a hard challenge, solved within hours (see [this tutorial](/tutorials/solve-market-split-problem-with-iskay-quantum-optimizer)).                                        | S: 1<br/>M: 5<br/>L: 15 |\n"
"| Singularity Machine Learning<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/multiverse-computing-singularity)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/multiverse-computing-singularity/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/oe621o30gxvpo8v0tivp31075w9wc6t8)  | Multiverse Computing | Classical machine learning classification workflows that could benefit from improved accuracy or computational efficiency by leveraging quantum optimization executed on IBM hardware.               | Delivers accuracy comparable to or exceeding classical models such as Random Forest or XGBoost, while operating with significantly fewer learners and a more compact ensemble. <br/><br/>Powered by quantum-optimized voting, it selects the most informative learners and refines decision boundaries, resulting in greater efficiency, reduced model complexity, and more robust performance. | N/A |\n"
"| Optimization Solver<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/q-ctrl-optimization-solver)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/q-ctrl-optimization-solver/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/ly9cs0lxy6nxqrirt5rt1xisnmvydj9z)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/q-ctrl-functions-eula.pdf)             | Q-CTRL               | Binary optimization problems or any combinatorial problem that can be mapped to a binary cost function.  <br/><br/>Cost functions of any order and problem sizes up to the maximum device scale are supported. | Noise-aware, end-to-end quantum optimization solution that enables inputs of high-level problem definitions and automatically finds accurate solutions to classically challenging combinatorial problems on utility-scale quantum hardware. <br/><br/>It abstracts away complexity by handling error suppression, efficient mapping, and hybrid quantum-classical optimization to solve optimization tasks at full device scale without deep quantum expertise. | S: .5<br/> M: 5<br/>L: 10 |\n"
"| Dynamics Simulator<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/q-ctrl-dynamics-simulator)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/q-ctrl-dynamics-simulator/api-reference)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/q-ctrl-functions-eula.pdf) | Q-CTRL | Time evolution of quantum many-body models, starting with one-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard chains, to study how spin, charge, and correlations propagate. | Accepts a physical model, initial state, time-evolution parameters, and observables instead of circuits, then builds, optimizes, and runs the circuits with Fire Opal's automated error suppression. <br/><br/>Agrees with high-resolution classical tensor-network simulations to within 1% RMSE, with quantum runtimes up to 3000 times faster. | S: .5<br/> M: 5<br/>L: 10 |\n"
"| Parity Twine Optimizer<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/parity-twine-optimizer)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/parity-twine-optimizer/api-reference)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/parityqc-parity-twine-optimizer-eula.pdf) | ParityQC | Optimization workloads that benefit from reduced gate counts and circuit depth, enabling industry-relevant problem sizes that are unfeasible with standard, SWAP-heavy transpilation methods. | Uses the Parity Twine method, built on the Parity Architecture, to minimize two-qubit gate counts and circuit depth while accounting for device connectivity, implementing non-local interactions without SWAP gates. <br/><br/>Automates transpilation steps with minimal user input and uses an efficient depth-one QAOA approach to obtain optimal circuit parameters on a CPU, minimizing required QPU runtime. | S: 1<br/>M: 10<br/>L: 15 |\n"
"| Constrained Quantum Optimizer<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer/api-reference)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer-eula.pdf) | Aqarios | Constrained binary optimization problems supplied as an LP file, MPS file, or Luna model, particularly those with one-hot or set-packing constraints. | Solves constrained binary optimization problems directly, enforcing one-hot and set-packing constraints natively through XY-mixers instead of penalty terms, which reduces the search space to the feasible subspace and improves solution quality. <br/><br/>Automatically handles reformulation, circuit synthesis, transpilation, and hardware execution using iterative warm-starting of the FlexQAOA algorithm, without variational parameter training. | S: 0.5<br/>M: 2<br/>L: 3.5 |\n"
"| Rimay Quantum Feature Extraction<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/kipu-rimay)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/kipu-rimay/api-reference)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/kipu-quantum-functions-eula.pdf) | Kipu Quantum | Drop-in feature extraction for classical machine learning pipelines. Leverage for small- and medium-sized tabular datasets, such as credit risk classification, where prediction quality has plateaued. | Extracts quantum-transformed features from your dataset. <br/><br/> Generated by digitized counterdiabatic evolution of a spin-glass Hamiltonian that encodes the data, as one preprocessing step, without building quantum circuits yourself. | S: 1<br/>M: 5<br/>L: 15 |\n"
"| SQOA Solver<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/jij-sqoa-solver/api-reference)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/jij-sqoa-solver-eula.pdf) | JIJ | Large combinatorial optimization problems formulated as QUBOs, including constrained problems converted with the penalty method, such as maximum independent set and MaxCut. | Uses quantum relaxation to encode up to three binary variables per qubit, so it can solve problems with more variables than the available qubits. <br/><br/>Its sampling-based design, which combines Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) with sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) and classical postprocessing, makes it less sensitive to hardware noise. | S: .5<br/> M: 1<br/>L: 2 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Nombre | Proveedor | Uso recomendado | Beneficios únicos | Costo por ejecución (RUs) |\n"
